### POST Request to Create Multi-choice Question

This endpoint allows you to create a multi-choice question for a specific course and user (teacher) email address.

#### Request Body

- `course_id` (text, required): The course ID.

- `email` (text, required): The user(teacher) email address.

- `questions[0][question]` (text, required): The question number 1.

- `questions[0][answer]` (text, required): The answer of question number 1.

- `questions[0][options][0]` (text, required): The answer option 1 of question number 1.

- `questions[0][options][1]` (text, required): The answer option 2 of question number 1.


#### Response

The response will contain the following JSON schema:

``` json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "status": {
      "type": "boolean"
    },
    "organisation_id": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "questions": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "question": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "answer": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "options": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

 ```

In case of an error, the response will include the following properties:

- `exception` (string): Details of any exceptions that occurred.

- `errorcode` (string): Error code, if applicable.

- `message` (string): Error message, if applicable.

- `debuginfo` (string): Additional debug information, if available.

### POST Request to Create True/False Questions

This endpoint allows you to create true/false questions for a specific course and user (teacher) email address.

#### Request Body

- `course_id` (text, required): The course ID.

- `email` (text, required): The user (teacher) email address.

- `questions[0][question]` (text, required): The question number 1.

- `questions[0][answer]` (text, required): The answer of question number 1; Accept: 0=false, 1=true.

- `questions[1][question]` (text, required): The question number 2.

- `questions[1][answer]` (text, required): The answer of question number 2; Accept: 0=false, 1=true.


#### Response

The response will contain the following JSON schema:

``` json
{
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
        "status": {
            "type": "boolean"
        },
        "organisation_id": {
            "type": "string"
        },
        "questions": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                    "question": {
                        "type": "string"
                    },
                    "answer": {
                        "type": "boolean"
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

 ```

In the response:

- `status` (boolean): Indicates the status of the request.

- `organisation_id` (string): The ID of the organization, if applicable.

- `questions` (array): An array of question objects with the following properties:

    - `question` (string): The question.

    - `answer` (boolean): The answer to the question.


In case of an error, the response will include the following properties:

- `exception` (string): Details of any exceptions that occurred.

- `errorcode` (string): Error code, if applicable.

- `message` (string): Error message, if applicable.

- `debuginfo` (string): Additional debug information, if available.
